# Root .gitignore for the AnyJersey project.
#
# Pattern scoping matters here, because the repo holds a Python toolchain and two Node
# apps side by side. A pattern with no slash — or only a trailing one — matches at every
# depth, so `node_modules/` covers the root, the backend and the storefront alike. A
# pattern with an interior slash is anchored to this file's directory, which is why the
# path-specific rules below spell out their full path from the repo root.
#
# This is the only .gitignore in the project, and deliberately so. The Medusa backend and
# the Next storefront each shipped one of their own, plus spike/ and tools/publish/; four
# files covering one tree meant a rule could be tightened in one and missed in the others
# — spike/backend/.gitignore ignored .env and .env.local but not .env.test, which is the
# exact shape of that bug. Every pattern those four held is reproduced below.
#
# The cost of consolidating is that patterns are no longer relative to the app they
# concern, so anything app-specific has to name its path from the repo root. Those are
# grouped and commented where they appear.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and environment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deny every .env by default, then re-admit only the files that are documentation rather
# than configuration. A newly added variable therefore cannot reach the repo unless
# somebody puts it in a template on purpose.
.env
.env.*
!.env.template
!.env.*.template
!.env.example
# Local-only values (localhost ports, JWT_SECRET=test) plus the comments recording why
# the integration runner reads DB_* and not just DATABASE_URL. Committed so a fresh clone
# can run the integration suite. Real credentials must never go in it.
!.env.test

# Keys and certificates, whatever they are called.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ~1.2 GB across the three package roots.
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.*
# The project standardises on npm: root CI, all three backend Dockerfile stages and the
# storefront build all run `npm ci`. Yarn's lockfile, .yarnrc.yml and pinned 4.12 release
# were deleted rather than left to drift, so any .yarn/ that reappears is accidental.
.yarn/
# The npm lockfiles are deliberately absent from this file: `npm ci` fails without them.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output and tool caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
.next/
.medusa/
.turbo/
.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo
# Rewritten by next dev/next build on every run.
next-env.d.ts
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# Medusa's local upload target: store content, not source.
spike/backend/static/
# Next's static-export target. Named in full to keep it distinct from tools/out.
spike/storefront/out/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated data and intermediates
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# extract.py output — 42 MB of CSVs plus a 15 MB live-products.json, all rebuildable
# from the backup archive. tools/README.md says to ignore it.
tools/out/
# md2html.py intermediates; build.py turns these into leaving-shopify.html.
tools/publish/body.html
tools/publish/toc.html
# Built by tools/build_import_json.py from the 2026-08-18 backup archive, which lives
# outside the repo (~/Downloads). A clone therefore cannot rebuild these and cannot seed
# until the archive is present — the import path is documented in tools/README.md.
spike/backend/src/scripts/catalog.json
spike/backend/src/scripts/catalog-sync.json

# Scratch state written by the spike runner.
spike/spike-state.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs and runtime noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.pid

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared editor settings are worth having in the repo; the rest of .vscode is personal.
**/.vscode/*
!**/.vscode/settings.json
!**/.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Per-machine Claude Code overrides. .claude/settings.json stays shared.
.claude/settings.local.json
